# core.autocrlf is true in this repository, which means git rewrites line
# endings on checkout for anything it considers text. That is fine for source.
# It is NOT fine for a vendored conformance corpus: a test file's bytes ARE the
# test. html5lib-tests holds cases whose expected output contains a bare \r, and
# WPT holds encoding and parsing tests that assert on exact byte sequences -- a
# corpus rewritten to CRLF measures the checkout instead of the browser, and
# does it silently, as a plausible-looking wall of failures.
#
# -text = never convert, in either direction.
third_party/wpt/** -text
third_party/html5lib-tests/** -text
